      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.74,
          "end": 1.58,
          "en": "Hi everyone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.58,
          "end": 5.81,
          "en": "So from this lecture we'll be focusing on queue and jobs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.84,
          "end": 12.71,
          "en": "Now I know you are familiar with queue term because we already used queue in our email sending feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.71,
          "end": 19.43,
          "en": "When we discussed about email sending, we also discussed about the basics of queue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 19.49,
          "end": 24.35,
          "en": "Now let me give you again the introduction of queue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 24.38,
          "end": 26.48,
          "en": "What is queue in Laravel?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 26.51,
          "end": 33.68,
          "en": "Queues provides a powerful way to defer the processing of a time consuming task, such as sending email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 33.98,
          "end": 39.89,
          "en": "I mean sending email or processing an upload uploaded file until a later time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 40.1,
          "end": 47.57,
          "en": "This is typically useful for improving the performance of your application by handling such tasks asynchronously,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 48.32,
          "end": 53.33,
          "en": "so they don't block the main execution flow, right.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 53.39,
          "end": 54.68,
          "en": "Email sending.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 54.95,
          "end": 57.65,
          "en": "Uploading big files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 57.65,
          "end": 59.21,
          "en": "Those type of stuff.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 59.24,
          "end": 60.2,
          "en": "Take time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 60.2,
          "end": 66.16,
          "en": "So what we can do via queue, we can do them in background in our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 66.76,
          "end": 70.45,
          "en": "So that in the user side user get a faster experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 70.45,
          "end": 73.24,
          "en": "Otherwise it will block our execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 73.81,
          "end": 80.23,
          "en": "If we upload a file or if we are sending an email in that time, it will block the execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 80.26,
          "end": 81.4,
          "en": "Code execution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 81.4,
          "end": 88.63,
          "en": "Until the email sending is completed, it will not, uh, proceed the code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 89.17,
          "end": 91.87,
          "en": "And user will see some sort of loading state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 91.9,
          "end": 95.56,
          "en": "Obviously mail sending takes time, so until then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 95.59,
          "end": 98.47,
          "en": "User have to sit there and wait for sending the mail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 98.47,
          "end": 101.2,
          "en": "But if we use queue what will happen?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 101.22999999999999,
          "end": 105.34,
          "en": "It will give the user response quickly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 105.34,
          "end": 108.55,
          "en": "It will not wait for sending the email, it will do it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 108.58,
          "end": 114.37,
          "en": "In background email will go to the user or I mean email will send successfully but user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 114.4,
          "end": 117.37,
          "en": "Don't have to wait in the frontend portion.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 117.37,
          "end": 122.95,
          "en": "So in any kind of time consuming task that will take time to execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 122.98,
          "end": 126.79,
          "en": "We use Q for handle those kind of tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 126.88,
          "end": 130.48,
          "en": "Now there is another term which is called chops.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 131.08,
          "end": 133.69,
          "en": "Now what is this chops.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 135.76,
          "end": 142.3,
          "en": "Now you can say, uh, in Laravel we call queues a little bit fancy way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 142.3,
          "end": 146.29,
          "en": "We call them jobs because we can create jobs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 146.32,
          "end": 150.31,
          "en": "A jobs represents a task that you want to defer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 150.34,
          "end": 157.15,
          "en": "Jobs can, uh, can any anything from sending email to processing data in Laravel.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 157.57,
          "end": 164.62,
          "en": "Jobs are usually stored in jobs jobs table or handled by queue driver.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 164.62,
          "end": 172.69,
          "en": "So basically, uh, normally we can do the queue, but there is a organized way to queuing your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 172.72,
          "end": 176.89,
          "en": "You can create a job class and in there you will put all the instruction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 176.92000000000002,
          "end": 179.76,
          "en": "Let's say you are working with email sending.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 179.76,
          "end": 182.88,
          "en": "You want to send an email and you want to also do the queue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 182.91,
          "end": 185.13,
          "en": "We already saw that how to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 185.13,
          "end": 192.24,
          "en": "But there is an another organized way for mail sending for a specific mail sending.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 192.24,
          "end": 199.77,
          "en": "We can create a job for that specific task, and inside the job we can assign that task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 199.77,
          "end": 206.79,
          "en": "And when we will run the job, it will do the task, but it will do it in background via queue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 207.3,
          "end": 209.49,
          "en": "Uh, I mean, queue feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 210.6,
          "end": 216.51,
          "en": "Uh, I hope you got understand that, but if you didn't, it's totally fine, because when we will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 216.51,
          "end": 218.88,
          "en": "it in action, you will get a better idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 218.88,
          "end": 222.12,
          "en": "So that's pretty much it for the introduction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 222.12,
          "end": 223.62,
          "en": "I hope you got the idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 223.77,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "And I already explained you about the queue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 234.36,
          "en": "And jobs are pretty much similar, but just organize way to queue our stuff, so we'll be seeing those",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
